---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 11, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — Solace"
	description="Solace has no servers and collects no personal data. Read exactly what stays on your device, what syncs via your own iCloud, and what a BYOK AI provider sees."
	path="/privacy"
>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
		<h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

		<div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-neutral-300">
			<p>
				Solace is built to work without a backend. There is no Solace server, no analytics
				pipeline, and no account system — this policy explains exactly where your data goes
				instead.
			</p>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">What stays only on your device</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					Your Keychain-stored credentials (an optional cloud AI provider key and, if you set
					one, your own USDA FoodData Central key) never leave your device and are never
					included in iCloud sync, logs, crash reports, or analytics of any kind.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">What syncs via your iCloud account</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					Your profile (body stats, activity level, allergen and diet exclusions, scoring
					weights), your diary entries, and your AI provider configuration (excluding the key
					itself) sync across your devices using Apple's CloudKit, under your own iCloud
					account. Solace cannot access this data — it is stored in your personal iCloud
					container, the same as Photos or Notes.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Apple Health</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					If you opt in, Solace writes the calories and macros you log to Apple Health. This is
					one-way and write-only — Solace does not read existing Health data, and nothing you
					log to Health is sent anywhere else.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Camera and photos</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					The camera is used to scan barcodes and, if you choose, to capture a meal photo for AI
					estimation. Barcode scans are processed on-device. A meal photo is only sent off-device
					if you have explicitly enabled and configured a cloud AI provider (see below) — otherwise
					no photo ever leaves your phone.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Third-party data sources</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					Barcode lookups query <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org" class="text-emerald-400 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-emerald-300">Open Food Facts</a>,
					a crowd-sourced, non-commercial database, and generic food search queries the <a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov" class="text-emerald-400 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-emerald-300">USDA FoodData Central</a> API, a US government public-domain database.
					These lookups send only the barcode or search term you enter — no account or profile
					data is attached.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Optional cloud AI (bring your own key)</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					Photo-based meal estimation is optional and off by default. If you enable it, you
					supply your own AI provider endpoint, model, and API key, and Solace sends the photo
					you choose to log directly to that provider on your behalf. No embedded or
					Solace-operated AI key is ever used, and estimates are always shown as an editable
					draft — never saved automatically.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Changes to this policy</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					If this policy changes, the "last updated" date above will change and the new version
					will be published at this same URL.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Contact</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:contact@nandan.fyi" class="text-emerald-400 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-emerald-300">contact@nandan.fyi</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
